The problem is that our stateless services pods do not set any of this.  There is no hostname or subdomain as they are a stateless service replicaset.  This means that, normally, they are addressed by the kubernetes load balancer via the service name.  However, when implementing a custom load balancer, we get into a case that we use the pod's generated DNS name such that we can direct traffic to the specific pod rather than the generic service endpoint.

The subtle change here was to no longer have a PTR for the pod's IP address anymore, which breaks the dependency on the DNS record in that case.

The simplest change is to notice that there is no hostname and continue as before.

The code change would look like:

```
		for _, eps := range ep.Subsets {
			for _, addr := range eps.Addresses {
				if addr.IP == ip {
					var domain string
					// If the pod specifies a hostname (such as statefulset does), use the hostname to build PTR
					// However, in case where hostname is not set, containue to produce a PTR based on the pod address
					// This fixes the major regression: https://github.com/coredns/coredns/issues/7177
					if addr.Hostname != "" {
						domain = strings.Join([]string{addr.Hostname, ep.Index, Svc, k.primaryZone()}, ".")
					} else {
						domain = strings.Join([]string{endpointHostname(addr, k.endpointNameMode), ep.Index, Svc, k.primaryZone()}, ".")
					}
					svcs = append(svcs, msg.Service{Host: domain, TTL: k.ttl})
				}
			}
		}
```
